# jemdoc: menu{MENU}{oldnews.html}, notime
= Past News

== 2025
- Dec. 2025: We successfully organized the [https://ai4nextg.github.io/ First AI4NextG Workshop @ NeurIPS 2025]. All the talks are freely available [https://slideslive.com/39053613/ai-and-ml-for-nextgeneration-wireless-communications-and-networking-ai4nextg-neurips25?ref=account-222237-presentations online]. 
- Nov. 2025: [https://www.linkedin.com/in/yujiamu/ Yujia Mu] successfully defended her dissertation. Congratulations, Dr. Mu!
- Oct. 2025: Co-organzing [https://ai4ts.github.io/aaai2026 AAAI 2026 Workshop on AI for Time Series Analysis (AI4TS): Theory, Algorithms, and Applications].
- Sept. 2025: PhD student [https://chen-1031.github.io/ Zihan Chen] received the McVey Fellowship, and PhD student Wei Shen received the Wilson Bicentennial Grad Fellowship. Congratulations!
- Aug. 2025: Area Chair for AISTATS 2026 and ICLR 2026.
- Aug. 2025: Lead organizer for [https://ai4nextg.github.io/ AI4NextG Workshop @ NeurIPS'25]. Submission deadline: August 29, 2025. Check our website for more details.
- May 2025: I started the role of [https://www.spectrumx.org/news/nsf-spectrumx-working-groups-gain-new-leaders-from-northwestern-uva/ Deputy Director of Collaboration at SpectrumX].
- Feb. 2025: Welcome Danya Balakumaran Meenakumari (master) and Diana Lin (undergraduate) to our [group.html group]!
- Feb. 2025: Co-organzing [https://ai4ts.github.io/aaai2025 AAAI 2025 Workshop on Artificial Intelligence for Time Series Analysis (AI4TS): Theory, Algorithms, and Applications].
- Jan. 2025: Two papers accepted to [https://iclr.cc/ ICLR 2025] and two papers accepted to [https://aistats.org/aistats2025/ AISTATS 2025]. Topics include multi-armed bandits, RLHF, in-context learning, transformers, and differential privacy. See [topics.html publication] for details.
- Jan. 2025: The collaborative paper "[https://www.science.org/stoken/author-tokens/ST-1855/full Stereoscopic artificial compound eyes for spatiotemporal perception in three-dimensional space]" between Prof. Kyusang Lee's group and ours has been selected as the *Best Paper of 2024* of Science Robotics. Read the Engineering School news [https://engineering.virginia.edu/news-events/news/influential-robotics-journal-picks-uva-paper-best-2024 here].
- Jan. 2025: Our [https://arxiv.org/abs/2411.07600 paper] on transformer-based physical-layer wireless system design has been accepted to ICC 2025.
- Jan. 2025: PhD student [https://kerzb.github.io/ Zhoubin Kou] joins our [group.html group]. Welcome!

== 2024
- Oct. 2024: [https://peter-peng-w.github.io/ Peng Wang] joins our [group.html group]. He is in our CS department and co-advised by me and [https://jing-yang7.github.io/ Prof. Jing Yang].
- Sept. 2024: Three papers accepted to [https://neurips.cc/ NeurIPS 2024]. Topics include in-context learning, transformers, game theory, and prompt engineering in LLMs. See [topics.html publication] for details.
- Sept. 2024: Kun's accepted Asilomar 2024 paper /Average Reward Reinforcement Learning for Wireless Radio Resource Management/ is selected as a *finalist for the Best Student Paper Award*.
- Sept. 2024: Three new PhD students join our [group.html group]: Di Wu, Songwei Dong, and Zihao Liang. Welcome!
- May 2024: Our paper "[https://www.science.org/stoken/author-tokens/ST-1855/full Stereoscopic artificial compound eyes for spatiotemporal perception in three-dimensional space]" is featured on the front page of both [https://www.science.org/ Science] and [https://www.science.org/journal/scirobotics Science Robotics]. 
- May 2024: Our paper "FastGAS: Fast Graph-based Annotation Selection for In-Context Learning" is accepted to ACL 2024 Findings. 
- May 2024: I'm co-organizing two workshops in the upcoming [https://kdd2024.kdd.org/ KDD 2024 conference]. Please consider submitting your works!
-- [https://kdd-milets.github.io/milets2024/ The 10th Mining and Learning from Time Series Workshop: From Classical Methods to LLMs]
-- [https://nl2ql.github.io/ NL2code: Reasoning and Planing with LLM for Code Development]
- May 2024: Two papers accepted to ICML 2024. Congratulations Zihan!
- Apr. 2024: Our project "Privacy-preserving Synthetic Data Generation" has been selected for funding by the CCI CATAPULT program. Joint effort with [https://tianhao.wang/ Prof. Tianhao Wang].
- Apr. 2024: Received UVA Engineering Research Innovation Awards (RIA) on the project "Artificial Insect Eye for Spatiotemporal Perception and Cognition in 3D Space via Edge Computing". Joint effort with [https://engineering.virginia.edu/faculty/kyusang-lee Prof. Kyusang Lee].
- Apr. 2024: PhD student Zihan Chen won the 2024 ECE Department Ann Lee Brown Rookie of the Year Graduate Research Award. Congratulations!
- Apr. 2024: Our project titled "[https://www.nsf.gov/awardsearch/showAward?AWD_ID=2332060&HistoricalAwards=false Integrating Federated Split Neural Network with Artificial Stereoscopic Compound Eyes for Optical Flow Sensing in 3D Space with Precision]" is funded by NSF. 
- Jan. 2024: Wei's first paper has been accepted to AISTATS 2024 -- Congratulations!
- Jan. 2024: We are organizing [https://icc2024.ieee-icc.org/workshop/ws-34-3rd-workshop-next-generation-spectrum-sharing-technology The 3rd Workshop on Next Generation Spectrum Sharing Technology] in conjunction with IEEE ICC 2024 in Denver, CO, USA. Please consider submitting your work.


